-- title:
--   Local maximal order is the reduced-norm valuation ring
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is a maximal order in the following sense: $\Lambda$ contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, is finitely generated, spans $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and every submodule $\Lambda'$ with these four properties containing $\Lambda$ equals $\Lambda$. Let $v$ be a height-one prime of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$, with $v$-adic completion $v.\mathrm{adicCompletion}\ \mathbb{Q}$ and valuation ring $v.\mathrm{adicCompletionIntegers}\ \mathbb{Q}$, and assume every non-zero element of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} v.\mathrm{adicCompletion}\ \mathbb{Q}$ is a unit. Let $\varphi$ be a ring isomorphism from this base change onto the quaternion algebra over $v.\mathrm{adicCompletion}\ \mathbb{Q}$ with parameters the images of $a$ and $b$, satisfying $\varphi(z\otimes r)=r\cdot(z_{\mathrm{re}},z_{\mathrm{imI}},z_{\mathrm{imJ}},z_{\mathrm{imK}})$ coordinatewise for $z$ in the rational algebra and $r$ a completion scalar. Then for every $x$ in the base change, $x$ lies in the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $c$ a $v$-adic integer if and only if $\mathrm{nrd}(\varphi x)=(\varphi x)_{\mathrm{re}}^2-a(\varphi x)_{\mathrm{imI}}^2-b(\varphi x)_{\mathrm{imJ}}^2+ab(\varphi x)_{\mathrm{imK}}^2$ lies in the valuation ring of $v.\mathrm{adicCompletion}\ \mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   This is the local structure theorem for maximal orders at a place where the quaternion algebra is a division algebra: the $v$-adic completion of a maximal order is the valuation ring $\{x:\operatorname{nrd}(x)\text{ is a }v\text{-adic integer}\}$, the unique maximal order of the local division algebra. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, where coset graphs and Atkin–Lehner elements at the ramified prime are analysed through membership in the local box and its unit group.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsMaximalOrder_mem_localBox_iff_nrd_mem_adicCompletionIntegers_of_forall_isUnit.lean

